<p>Mitigating involuntary churn requires automated dunning pipelines. When a subscription charge fails, the system must execute smart card retries based on issuing bank processing schedules, send polite non-intrusive notification emails with one-click payment update links, and provide grace periods before restricting account access.</p>
<p>For voluntary churn, tracking in-app engagement drops—such as an active user stopping their weekly publishing cadence—allows proactive intervention. Triggering personalized automated check-in emails from the founder frequently resolves user confusion before a cancellation is submitted.</p>
