<p>Leaving the bustling concourse of Kyoto behind, you transition through regional junction stations until you board a vintage single-car KiHa 40 diesel railcar painted in deep emerald and cream. Inside, the carriage features faded blue velour bench seats, wooden floor slats polished by generations of commuters, and openable windows with brass latches.</p>
