<p>There is profound peace in the endurance of stone. It reminds us that what truly matters in human culture are not the transient political controversies of the hour, but the durable monuments of beauty, hospitality, and shared truth that we leave behind for future generations.</p>
<p>By building our own work—whether physical architecture, written essays, or software systems—with the permanence and generous hospitality of the caravanserai, we participate in this noble, unbroken continuum of human craft.</p>
